WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.540
The DCEU has gone up in flames — and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.320
it seems, Warner Bros. has figured out&nbsp;
how to kill two films with one Rock.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.080
Dwayne Johnson spent most of the build-up to Black&nbsp;
Adam teasing that the hierarchy of the DC universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.480
was about to change — but his ambitious dreams for&nbsp;
the franchise have seemingly been dashed. On the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.160
heels of Black Adam's poor reception, Shazam!&nbsp;
Fury of the Gods has been met with largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.440
negative reviews and poor box office takings.&nbsp;
Ironically, none other than Johnson himself could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.840
be to blame for the DCEU's recent misfortunes,&nbsp;
as he allegedly meddled behind the scenes.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.140
A report by The Wrap details&nbsp;
how Johnson pushed back against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.920
Black Adam and Shazam crossing&nbsp;
paths on screen. Most notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.380
he apparently vetoed a Black Adam post-credits&nbsp;
scene in which Zachary Levi's Shazam joins the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.120
Justice Society of America. This stinger was&nbsp;
eventually used in Shazam! Fury of the Gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.100
but The Wrap says Johnson blocked any potential&nbsp;
appearances from his Black Adam co-stars.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.900
This is just the latest example of Johnson&nbsp;
interfering with the DCEU. Back when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.280
first Shazam! movie was in development, Black&nbsp;
Adam was set to have a key role. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.360
Johnson convinced Warner Bros. to make&nbsp;
a standalone Black Adam film instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.960
feeling it would be a disservice to&nbsp;
his character if Shazam! featured a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.460
pair of origin stories. Despite the characters'&nbsp;
close connection to each other in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.240
Shazam and Black Adam made their big&nbsp;
screen debuts separate from each other.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.800
While some may have thought the two would meet&nbsp;
in a future installment, Johnson seemingly had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.840
other ideas. He infamously strong-armed Warner&nbsp;
Bros. into approving a Black Adam cameo for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.829
Henry Cavill's Superman, setting the stage for&nbsp;
a massive fight between those two characters.

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:40.193
"Black Adam… We should talk."

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:46.020
Throughout the Black Adam press&nbsp;
tour, Johnson continuously hyped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.980
up such a confrontation. By downplaying&nbsp;
Black Adam's strong links to Shazam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:55.080
Johnson unwittingly hamstrung two comic book&nbsp;
franchises. An argument can be made that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.820
if he used his platform and influence to drum&nbsp;
up anticipation for Shazam vs. Black Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:04.200
these two properties could have had a&nbsp;
bright future — instead of being shelved.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.640
Now, it looks like all of these characters&nbsp;
will likely be either taking a long hiatus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.620
or getting flushed from the DCU altogether&nbsp;
to make room for the whole slate of new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:19.140
characters. This has got to come as a major blow&nbsp;
to Warner Bros. Discovery. The first Shazam! was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.180
both a critical and financial success, netting a&nbsp;
score of 90% on Rotten Tomatoes and bringing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:31.020
$366 million on its estimated budget of just&nbsp;
$100 million. Meanwhile, Shazam! Fury of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.660
Gods debuted with $30.1 million domestically,&nbsp;
bringing in less than half of its hefty budget.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.520
To complicate matters further, new heroes&nbsp;
like Blue Beetle are set to join the DCEU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.200
If The Flash and Blue Beetle do well for&nbsp;
Warner Bros. Discovery, it seems unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.580
that James Gunn and Peter Safran will see&nbsp;
any reason to bring back failed characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.780
especially with so many other DCEU&nbsp;
heroes already on the chopping block.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.460
Although Dwayne Johnson has long been thought to&nbsp;
be one of the biggest box office draws around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.600
his meddling with the DCEU may&nbsp;
have tanked a shared three-movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.380
franchise. What that means for&nbsp;
his career remains to be seen.

